WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.640
Hey, John.

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:01.770
My name is not Hank.

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:02.510
Who the eff is Hank?

00:00:02.510 --> 00:00:05.860
Well, to that I say, clean up your language,
young person.

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:06.700
Or old person.

00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:07.470
Or middle person.

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:10.280
No, my name is Craig, AKA WheezyWaiter on
the intertubes.

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:13.999
That’s right, if you ever see me on a lazy
river riding in an intertube, call me WheezyWaiter.

00:00:13.999 --> 00:00:18.259
A few years ago, I filled in for you, John,
and I did my best impression of you that I could.

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:19.400
It was well received.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:23.020
Roger Ebert of the Chicago Sun Times said,
“Two thumbs up!” several times throughout

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:24.220
his career about other things.

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:29.040
Anyway, if any of you nerdfighters miss Hank
right now, I will do some things that Hank does.

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:30.050
Dancing.

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:34.940
You gotta do a lot of hip thrusts when you hip
dance like Hank.

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:36.500
He also sings rock music.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:37.700
Rock music!

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:39.080
Yeah.

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:40.210
What else does he do?

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:41.370
Breathing.

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:45.210
Pooping, I’m assuming, and other stuff.

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:49.210
He also smiles when he talks, then he talks
like this sometimes when he’s trying to

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:50.170
get his words out.

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:52.280
You know what I’m talking about, John.

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:55.680
So, all bad impressions aside, right now we
are celebrating Pizzamas.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:01:00.000
In honor of me trying to be like Hank, I’m
going to tell you about the science of pizza.

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:04.380
The term “pizza” first appeared in a Latin
text around the 10th century in southern Italy.

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:07.720
Here’s a reenactment: Let’s call it pizza!

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:11.130
I learned everything about my Italian accent
from Mario 64.

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:11.970
Let’s go!

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:16.610
The Latin text was found in the town of Gaeta,
Italy, and it stated that a person of a certain

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:21.580
property is to give the bishop of Gaeta twelve
pizzas every day.

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:25.350
So basically, you have to give 12 pizzas to
the bishop if you are at a certain high income

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:28.320
level, or upper crust, if you will.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:29.560
I’m sorry.

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:30.620
I’m so sorry.

00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:34.040
Also, I just realized I’m talking about
the history of pizza and not the science of pizza.

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:35.740
History’s more your thing, John. I'm sorry.

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:36.920
Here’s the science of pizza.

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:37.940
Let’s go!

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:38.680
That’s the last time I’ll do that.

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:43.840
Most basic pizzas have three things—well,
four if you count joy—five if you count

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:50.030
bloating when you eat too much—but the three
are: bread, sauce, cheese.

00:01:50.030 --> 00:01:51.439
Why did I have to look at that?

00:01:51.439 --> 00:01:52.860
I have had pizza before?

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:57.450
The bread is made of flour, water, and baker’s
yeast, which is actually a living, single-celled

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:00.149
fungus called saccharomyces cerevisiae.

00:02:00.149 --> 00:02:03.840
Yeah, I said a big word. That means I got to the science.

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:05.060
Boom! Scienced! Moving on.

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:09.380
And, of course, a crucial element of Pizza
John is the Pizza John mustache.

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:11.380
So, here’s the history of the mustache.

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:16.000
The oldest portrait of a mustache is an Iranian
horseman from 300 AD—BC.

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:17.240
BC.

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:17.940
Not AD.

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:18.480
BC.

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:21.640
I couldn’t find the photo, but I imagine
it looked something like this.

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:24.260
By “horseman” I assume they meant “centaur.”

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:26.840
And by “photo” I assume they meant “sewn
to a pillow.”

00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:28.270
That is all I have for you today.

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:29.660
I assume you learned nothing.

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:31.470
Thank you Hank and John for having me.

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:32.470
I love doing these.

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:33.620
Please have lots more kids.

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:34.700
I’ll see you sometime.

